...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI. R SRINIVASA GOWDA, AGA FOR R1;
 SRI. B B PATIL, ADVOCATE FOR R3;
 V.C.O DATED 23.02.2016, WP IS DISMISSED AGAINST R4)
 THIS WRIT PETITION IS FILED UNDER ARTICLES 226 AND 227 OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA, PRAYING TO DECLARE THAT THE ACQUISITION IN RESPECT OF PETITION LAND SY.NO.40/342 MEASURING 1 ACRE SITUATED AT BANDIKODIGHALLI VILLAGE, JALA HOBLI, BANGALORE NORTH TALUK IN PURSUANCE OF THE PRELIMINARY AND FINAL NOTIFICATIONS DATED 3.11.2006 AND 7.5.2007 RESPECTIVELY VIDE ANN-D & E.
 THIS PETITION COMING ON FOR FINAL HEARING THIS DAY, THE COURT MADE THE FOLLOWING:
 ORDER Petitioner claiming to be the owner of the subject land, is knocking at the doors of Writ Court for assailing the KIADB acquisition that commenced with the issuance of Preliminary Notification dated 4.11.2006 u/s 28(1) followed by Final Notification dated 7.5.2007 u/s 28(4) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act, 1966.

opennyai_summary.ANALYSIS:
Since the acquisition under 1966 Act is khata-specific as held by this court in a catena of decisions, the acquisition notifications cannot be faltered on the ground that it did not mention the name of petitioner when petitioner's name did not figure in the khata at all.
(b) The Preliminary Notification u/s 28(1) of the 1966 Act was issued on 4.11.2006;
petitioner not being the khatedar, obviously did not and could not file the objections and that cannot be helped at this length of time; the Final Notification u/s 28(4) was issued on 7.5.2007.
